From 60a2d43058344dbcb327bc0d5f6262bb9deec71d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:57:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] yadif arm: NEON line filter for 32-bit ARM (8 bits a
 sample)

Bit-exact with filter_line_c: eight pixels an iteration, sums and scores
in 16 bits, the averages with vhadd. Byte-element loads and stores only,
so it needs no alignment (RISC OS traps unaligned wider accesses). Like
the x86 versions it may read 2 bytes and write up to 7 pixels past w,
which vf_yadif.c leaves room for (filter_edges writes the right-hand
pixels afterwards).
---
